From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: 8 bpc at most

msm_dp_panel_get_supported_bpp() picks the deepest colour the link can
carry, up to 10 bpc, from what the EDID claims (12 bpc on the LG
UltraGear+). Every framebuffer on this device has 8 bits a channel and
a monitor gets no colour profile, so 10 bpc only carried padding. Stop
at 8; modes that need it still fall back to 6.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -215,7 +215,11 @@
 		u32 mode_edid_bpp, u32 mode_pclk_khz)
 {
 	const struct msm_dp_link_info *link_info;
-	const u32 max_supported_bpp = 30, min_supported_bpp = 18;
+	/*
+	 * 8 bpc at most: every framebuffer here has 8 bits a channel and a
+	 * monitor gets no colour profile, so 10 bpc only carried padding.
+	 */
+	const u32 max_supported_bpp = 24, min_supported_bpp = 18;
 	u32 bpp, data_rate_khz;
 
 	bpp = min(mode_edid_bpp, max_supported_bpp);
